            <ArticleTitle>An Overview of Currently Available Antimalarials.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2143-2157</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2174/1568026617666170130123520</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND">Despite the substantial progress over the time, malaria remains a major public health concern and causing hundreds of thousands of deaths. Resistance to the available antimalarial therapy increases threat to the global public health.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE">Overview of currently available antimalarials.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHOD">Literary survey.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS">The summarized data about different types of antimalarial therapies and their efficiency and modes of action.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION">Despite the seemingly large number of the drugs currently available for malaria treatment, this arsenal is limited due to the narrow variation of their mechanism of action.</AbstractText>
